<title>SPAIN: Spain's ENCE 1996 net loss 2.95 bln ptas.</title>
<headline>Spain's ENCE 1996 net loss 2.95 bln ptas.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish paper firm ENCE said on Friday it made a net loss of 2.95 billion pesetas in 1996 compared with a profit of 12.79 billion pesetas in 1995.</p>
<p>Results were badly hit by an average fall in cellulose prices of 44 percent during the year, which had an adverse effect of 19.7 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>Cardboard sales rose by 4.3 percent from a year earlier to 572,000 tonnes, while fixed production costs fell three percent.</p>
<p>The company said it had bank debts of some 11.46 billion.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
